# SIT210 Embedded Systems Development.
# Smart Wearable Fall Detection and Caregiver Monitoring System

## Overview

It is a Smart Wearable Fall Detection and Caregiver Monitoring System designed to help detect possible falls and notify caregivers in real time.

The patient-side wearable device uses an Arduino Nano 33 IoT with its built-in IMU sensor to detect fall-like movement. When a fall is confirmed, the system activates a local buzzer alarm and sends an MQTT emergency alert.

On the caregiver side, a Raspberry Pi with Node-RED receives the alert and updates a real-time monitoring dashboard. A patient assistance dashboard is also included for manual help requests and optional Telegram notifications.

---

## Hardware Used

- Arduino Nano 33 IoT
- Raspberry Pi
- Buzzer
- Slider switch
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires
- Portable power bank

---

## Software Used

- Arduino IDE
- Node-RED
- MQTT Broker (broker.emqx.io)
- Arduino Libraries:
  - Arduino_LSM6DS3
  - WiFiNINA
  - PubSubClient
- Telegram (optional integration)

---

## Files in this Repository

- `wearable_fall_detection.ino` – Arduino code for wearable fall detection system
- `caregiver_dashboard.json` – Node-RED caregiver monitoring dashboard flow
- `patient_dashboard.json` – Node-RED patient assistance dashboard flow
- `README.md` – Project documentation
